<title>CHINA: NATIONAL ELEC YR NET RISES 64 PCT.</title>
<headline>NATIONAL ELEC YR NET RISES 64 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	  7.7	   vs 4.6</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)   2.6	   vs 2.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	 201.75 gain vs 111.18 gain</p>
<p>    Net			   94.73	 vs 57.76</p>
<p>    Turnover		    1,774.75    vs 1,532.25</p>
<p>    Company name		National Electronics Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		 September 22-29</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	  September 30</p>
<p>NOTE - National Electronics invests in property and makes electronic watches and telecommunications equipment.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain on disposal of long-term property interests, investment properties land and buildings.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 5.2 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of 1.3 cents and special dividend of 1.3 cents) vs 3.3 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843 6368</p>
